# Materials module (P7) — demo requests (VS / Rider / VS Code REST Client).
#
# One-time local setup (Development) is the same as users.http. Uploaded files go to App_Data/files next to the host
# (Storage:RootPath); that folder is git-ignored.
# Prerequisites: scheduling.http + lifecycle.http (active term, a subject the professor teaches, a registered student).

@host = http://localhost:5080
@adminToken = paste-the-admin-token-here
@professorToken = paste-the-teaching-professors-token-here
@studentToken = paste-a-registered-students-token-here
@subjectId = paste-a-subject-id-here
@materialId = paste-the-id-from-the-upload-here

### Professor: upload a PDF (multipart) → 201 (allowed: pdf ppt pptx doc docx xls xlsx zip png jpg jpeg mp4, ≤ 50 MB)
POST {{host}}/api/materials
Authorization: Bearer {{professorToken}}
Content-Type: multipart/form-data; boundary=NIMI

--NIMI
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="subjectId"

{{subjectId}}
--NIMI
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="title"

Lecture 3 — Graphs
--NIMI
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="weekNumber"

3
--NIMI
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="file"; filename="graphs.pdf"
Content-Type: application/pdf

%PDF-1.7 demo
--NIMI--

### Student (registered) or professor (teaching) or admin: the subject's materials this term
GET {{host}}/api/materials?subjectId={{subjectId}}&weekNumber=3
Authorization: Bearer {{studentToken}}

### Download (counts the download; invisible or deleted → 404)
GET {{host}}/api/materials/{{materialId}}/download
Authorization: Bearer {{studentToken}}

### Uploader / teacher: edit the metadata (the file never changes)
PUT {{host}}/api/materials/{{materialId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{professorToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "title": "Lecture 3 — Graphs (updated)", "description": "With exercises", "weekNumber": 3 }

### Uploader / teacher: soft delete → 204 (the stored file is kept)
DELETE {{host}}/api/materials/{{materialId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{professorToken}}
